###  http://data.europa.eu/949/conditionalRegenerativeBrake
:conditionalRegenerativeBrake rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                              rdfs:subPropertyOf :trackObjParameter ,
                                                 :trackResistanceToAppliedLoadsObjParameter ;
                              rdf:type owl:FunctionalProperty ;
                              rdfs:domain :ContactLineSystem ;
                              rdfs:range <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> ;
                              :XMLName "ECS_RegenerativeBraking" ;
                              :applicable "Y/N" ;
                              :dependencyNote "When `not electrified` is chosen in parameter 1.1.1.2.2.1.1, then this parameter is not applicable. "@en ;
                              :inSkosConceptScheme <http://data.europa.eu/949/concepts/regenerative-braking/RegenerativeBraking> ;
                              :legalDeadline "In accordance with Implementing Decision 2014/880/EU and by 16 March 2019 at the latest"@en ;
                              :rinfIndex "1.1.1.2.2.4" ;
                              :shaclShapeValidationRule <http://data.europa.eu/949/shapes/ConditionalRegenerativeBrake> ,
                                                        <http://data.europa.eu/949/shapes/ConditionalRegenerativeBrakeSKOS> ;
                              :tsiOPEAppendixD2Index "3.3.7" ;
                              :usedInRCCCalculations "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
                              <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2020-08-24"^^xsd:date ;
                              <http://purl.org/dc/terms/modified> "2023-01-20"^^xsd:date ,
                                                                  "2024-09-25"^^xsd:date ,
                                                                  "2024-12-10"^^xsd:date ,
                                                                  "2025-02-28"^^xsd:date ;
                              <http://purl.org/dc/terms/relation> :contactLineSystemType ;
                              rdfs:comment "Indication whether regenerative braking is permitted, not permitted, or permitted under specific conditions."@en ;
                              rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://data.europa.eu/949/> ;
                              rdfs:label "Permission for regenerative braking"@en ;
                              <http://www.w3.org/2003/06/sw-vocab-status/ns#term_status> "stable" ;
                              <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> """When regenerative braking is \"allowed under conditions\", a document must be provided under 1.1.1.2.2.4.1.

For RINF XML data sets:
As long as the data provision through XML data sets is allowed, an XML attribute called â€œSetâ€ will be used to link the value of this parameter to the parameter 1.1.1.2.2.1.1 / ECS_SystemType"""@en .


###  http://data.europa.eu/949/conditionsAppliedRegenerativeBraking
:conditionsAppliedRegenerativeBraking rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                      rdfs:subPropertyOf :contactLineSystemObjParameter ;
                                      rdf:type owl:FunctionalProperty ;
                                      rdfs:domain :ContactLineSystem ;
                                      rdfs:range :Document ;
                                      :applicable "Y/N/NYA" ;
                                      :dependencyNote "When `not electrified` is chosen in parameter 1.1.1.2.2.1.1, then this parameter is not applicable. Mandatory when parameter 1.1.1.2.2.4 announces Conditions."@en ;
                                      :legalDeadline "12 months after publication of Article 7 Guide"@en ;
                                      :rinfIndex "1.1.1.2.2.4.1" ;
                                      :shaclShapeValidationRule <http://data.europa.eu/949/shapes/ConditionsAppliedRegenerativeBraking> ,
                                                                <http://data.europa.eu/949/shapes/ConditionsAppliedRegenerativeBrakingApplicability> ;
                                      :tsiOPEAppendixD2Index "3.3.7" ;
                                      <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2022-11-10"^^xsd:date ;
                                      <http://purl.org/dc/terms/modified> "2023-03-14"^^xsd:date ,
                                                                          "2024-04-18"^^xsd:date ,
                                                                          "2024-11-04"^^xsd:date ,
                                                                          "2025-02-28"^^xsd:date ;
                                      <http://purl.org/dc/terms/relation> :contactLineSystemType ;
                                      <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <http://data.europa.eu/eli/reg_impl/2019/773/oj> ,
                                                                        <http://data.europa.eu/eli/reg_impl/2019/777/2023-09-28> ;
                                      rdfs:comment "Name and/or reference of the document specifying the conditions applying in regards to regenerative braking."@en ;
                                      rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://data.europa.eu/949/> ;
                                      rdfs:label "Conditions applying in regards to regenerative braking"@en ;
                                      <http://www.w3.org/2003/06/sw-vocab-status/ns#term_status> "stable" ;
                                      <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> """The value of this parameter should be either a reference to a file name or an external link to a document.
If a file name is provided, the Infrastructure Manager (IM) must upload a document with the same file name using the \"Reference Documents Management\" functionality in the RINF application. The document must be in electronic format and available in two official EU languages. In this case, the parameter value must be repeated for each document.
If an external link is provided, the IM must ensure that the document is available at the provided link."""@en .


###  http://data.europa.eu/949/conditionsSwitchClassBSystems
:conditionsSwitchClassBSystems rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                               rdfs:subPropertyOf :transitionsBetweenSystemsObjParameter ;
                               rdf:type owl:FunctionalProperty ;
                               rdfs:domain [ rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                             owl:unionOf ( :CommonCharacteristicsSubset
                                                           :RunningTrack
                                                         )
                                           ] ;
                               rdfs:range :Document ;
                               :applicable "Y/N/NYA" ;
                               :dependencyNote "Applicable when at least two different class of protection systems exist."@en ;
                               :legalDeadline "12 months after publication of Article 7 Guide"@en ;
                               :rinfIndex "1.1.1.3.8.3" ,
                                          "1.2.1.1.7.3" ;
                               :shaclShapeValidationRule <http://data.europa.eu/949/shapes/ConditionsSwitchClassBSystems> ,
                                                         <http://data.europa.eu/949/shapes/ConditionsSwitchClassBSystemsApplicability> ;
                               :tsiOPEAppendixD2Index "3.4.3" ;
                               <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2022-10-28"^^xsd:date ;
                               <http://purl.org/dc/terms/modified> "2023-03-14"^^xsd:date ,
                                                                   "2024-04-18"^^xsd:date ,
                                                                   "2024-11-04"^^xsd:date ,
                                                                   "2025-02-28"^^xsd:date ;
                               <http://purl.org/dc/terms/relation> :ETCS ,
                                                                   :switchProtectControlWarning ;
                               <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <http://data.europa.eu/eli/reg_impl/2019/773/oj> ,
                                                                 <http://data.europa.eu/eli/reg_impl/2023/1695/oj> ;
                               rdfs:comment "Name and/or reference of the document specifying the Special technical conditions required to switch over between ERTMS/ETCS and Class B systems."@en ;
                               rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://data.europa.eu/949/> ;
                               rdfs:label "Special technical conditions required to switch over between ERTMS/ETCS and Class B systems"@en ;
                               <http://www.w3.org/2003/06/sw-vocab-status/ns#term_status> "stable" ;
                               <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> """The details of the conditions to switch between Class B train protection systems must be published.

The value of this parameter should be either a reference to a file name or an external link to a document.
If a file name is provided, the Infrastructure Manager (IM) must upload a document with the same file name using the \"Reference Documents Management\" functionality in the RINF application. The document must be in electronic format and available in two official EU languages. In this case, the parameter value must be repeated for each document.
If an external link is provided, the IM must ensure that the document is available at the provided link."""@en .


###  http://data.europa.eu/949/conditionsUseReflectivePlates
:conditionsUseReflectivePlates rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                               rdfs:subPropertyOf :healthSafetyAndEnvironmentObjParameter ;
                               rdfs:domain [ rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                             owl:unionOf ( :CommonCharacteristicsSubset
                                                           :RunningTrack
                                                         )
                                           ] ;
                               rdfs:range <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> ;
                               :applicable "Y/N/NYA" ;
                               :dependencyNote "A value is mandatory if the value of parameter \"Permit of use of reflective plates\" is boolean \"Yes\""@en ;
                               :inSkosConceptScheme <http://data.europa.eu/949/concepts/conditions-use-reflective-plates/ConditionsUseReflectivePlates> ;
                               :legalDeadline "12 months after publication of Article 7 Guide"@en ;
                               :rinfIndex "1.1.1.1.7.12.1" ;
                               :shaclShapeValidationRule <http://data.europa.eu/949/shapes/ConditionsUseReflectivePlates> ,
                                                         <http://data.europa.eu/949/shapes/ConditionsUseReflectivePlatesSKOS> ;
                               <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2023-03-14"^^xsd:date ;
                               <http://purl.org/dc/terms/modified> "2024-09-24"^^xsd:date ;
                               rdfs:comment "Details of any conditions for using the reflective plates on freight corridors. Specific case for Portugal and Spain until 1.1.2025 and Belgium and France until 1.1.2026."@en ;
                               rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://data.europa.eu/949/> ;
                               rdfs:label "Conditions for use of reflective plates"@en ;
                               rdfs:seeAlso "4.2.2.1.3.2 of TSI OPE (Commission Implementing Regulation (EU) 2019/773 of 16 May 2019)" ;
                               <http://www.w3.org/2003/06/sw-vocab-status/ns#term_status> "stable" ;
                               <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "From TSI OPE: Member States shall in particular endeavour to permit the use of reflective plates on rail freight corridors, with a view to prioritise the current bottlenecks. These sections and details of any conditions pertaining to them shall be recorded in the RINF. Until the information is encoded in RINF, the infrastructure manager shall ensure the information is communicated to railway undertakings by other appropriate means. The infrastructure manager shall identify the sections of lines on which 2 steady red lights are required in the RINF. "@en .


###  http://data.europa.eu/949/connectedTo
:connectedTo rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
             rdfs:subPropertyOf :trackGenericObjParameter ;
             rdf:type owl:SymmetricProperty ,
                      owl:IrreflexiveProperty ;
             rdfs:domain :Track ;
             rdfs:range :Track ;
             :applicable "Y/N/NYA" ;
             :legalDeadline "12 months after publication of Article 7 Guide"@en ;
             :rinfIndex "1.1.1.0.1.2" ,
                        "1.2.4.1" ;
             <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2025-03-10"^^xsd:date ;
             rdfs:comment "Represents a bidirectional connection between two Track instances."@en ;
             rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://data.europa.eu/949/> ;
             rdfs:label "connected to"@en ;
             rdfs:seeAlso :NetElement ,
                          :NetRelation ;
             <http://www.w3.org/2003/06/sw-vocab-status/ns#term_status> "stable" ;
             <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Internal connection"@en ,
                                                            "Tracks connectivity to operational points"@en ;
             <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "Track_A connectedTo Track_B implies Track_B connectedTo Track_A."@en ;
             <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> """This property defines a connection between two tracks. It is symmetric, meaning if a track A is connected to track B, then track B is also connected to track A. A track cannot be connected to itself (irreflexive property).
Used to indicate connectivity between track instances in a network, ensuring that connections are non-self-referential and in the normal running direction of the track.

This is a simplistic representation of the internal connectivity of the tracks in an operational point or the connectivity of the tracks between operational points and sections of line.
For a more detailed representation of connectivity and navigability, this information should be available on the topology of the network."""@en .


###  http://data.europa.eu/949/contactLineSystem
:contactLineSystem rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                   rdfs:domain [ rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                 owl:unionOf ( :CommonCharacteristicsSubset
                                               :RunningTrack
                                             )
                               ] ;
                   rdfs:range :ContactLineSystem ;
                   :shaclShapeValidationRule <http://data.europa.eu/949/shapes/ContactLineSystem> ;
                   <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2020-08-24"^^xsd:date ;
                   <http://purl.org/dc/terms/modified> "2021-09-11"^^xsd:date ,
                                                       "2025-02-28"^^xsd:date ;
                   rdfs:comment "System that is used to transmit electrical energy to road or rail vehicles."@en ;
                   rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://data.europa.eu/949/> ;
                   rdfs:label "contact line system"@en ;
                   <http://www.w3.org/2003/06/sw-vocab-status/ns#term_status> "stable" ;
                   <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> """It can be repeated as many times as the number of different contact line system types are present.

For RDF data provision:
The value of this property is an instance of the era:ContactLineSystem, which has as properties the parameters 1.1.1.2.2.1.2, 1.1.1.2.2.2, 1.1.1.2.2.4 and 1.1.1.2.5.1.

For RINF XML data sets:
As long as the data provision through XML data sets is allowed, this property is the equivalent of the \"Set\" attribute, grouping parameters 1.1.1.2.2.1.2, 1.1.1.2.2.2, 1.1.1.2.2.4 and 1.1.1.2.5.1."""@en .


###  http://data.europa.eu/949/contactLineSystemObjParameter
:contactLineSystemObjParameter rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                               rdfs:subPropertyOf :energySubsystemObjParameter ;
                               :rinfIndex "1.1.1.2.2" ;
                               <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2024-10-31"^^xsd:date ;
                               rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://data.europa.eu/949/> ;
                               rdfs:label "Contact line system"@en .


###  http://data.europa.eu/949/contactLineSystemType
:contactLineSystemType rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                       rdfs:subPropertyOf :contactLineSystemObjParameter ;
                       rdf:type owl:FunctionalProperty ;
                       rdfs:domain :ContactLineSystem ;
                       rdfs:range <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> ;
                       :XMLName "ECS_SystemType" ;
                       :applicable "Y/N" ;
                       :dependencyNote "If this parameter is repeated, parameters 1.1.1.2.2.1.2, and 1.1.1.2.2.2 shall be created also for the corresponding type. These two parameters are to be considered children of the current. "@en ;
                       :inSkosConceptScheme <http://data.europa.eu/949/concepts/contact-line-systems/ContactLineSystems> ;
                       :legalDeadline "In accordance with Implementing Decision 2014/880/EU and by 16 March 2019 at the latest"@en ;
                       :rinfIndex "1.1.1.2.2.1.1" ;
                       :shaclShapeValidationRule <http://data.europa.eu/949/shapes/ContactLineSystemType> ,
                                                 <http://data.europa.eu/949/shapes/ContactLineSystemTypeNotElectrifiedApplicability> ,
                                                 <http://data.europa.eu/949/shapes/ContactLineSystemTypeSKOS> ,
                                                 <http://data.europa.eu/949/shapes/ContactLineSystemTypeThirdOrFourthRailApplicability> ;
                       :usedInRCCCalculations "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
                       <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2021-08-06"^^xsd:date ;
                       <http://purl.org/dc/terms/modified> "2021-08-06"^^xsd:date ,
                                                           "2025-02-28"^^xsd:date ;
                       rdfs:comment "Indication of the type of the contact line system."@en ;
                       rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://data.europa.eu/949/> ;
                       rdfs:label "Type of contact line system"@en ;
                       <http://www.w3.org/2003/06/sw-vocab-status/ns#term_status> "stable" ;
                       <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> """When the value is \"not electrified\", then all parameters 1.1.1.2.2.1.2 - 1.1.1.2.5.3 are not applicable.
When the value is â€œThird Railâ€ or â€œFourth Railâ€, then parameters 1.1.1.2.2.3, 1.1.1.2.2.5 - 1.1.1.2.4.2.3, 1.1.1.2.5.2 and 1.1.1.2.5.3 are not applicable

For RINF XML data sets:
As long as the data provision through XML data sets is allowed, if this parameter is repeated, parameters 1.1.1.2.2.1.2, 1.1.1.2.2.2, 1.1.1.2.2.4 and 1.1.1.2.5.1 shall be created also for the corresponding type. These four parameters are to be considered children of the current.
For grouping â€œchildrenâ€ parameters of the current parameter, an XML attribute called â€œsetâ€ must be declared at the parent and children levels with the same keyword value."""@en .


###  http://data.europa.eu/949/contactStripMaterial
:contactStripMaterial rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                      rdfs:subPropertyOf :pantographObjParameter ,
                                         :vehicleTypeTechnicalObjectCharacteristic ;
                      rdf:type owl:FunctionalProperty ;
                      rdfs:domain [ rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                    owl:unionOf ( :CommonCharacteristicsSubset
                                                  :RunningTrack
                                                  :VehicleType
                                                )
                                  ] ;
                      rdfs:range <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> ;
                      :XMLName "EPA_StripMaterial" ;
                      :applicable "Y/N" ;
                      :dependencyNote "Mandatory only if â€œOverhead contact line (OCL)â€ is selected in 1.1.1.2.2.1.1, otherwise the parameter is not applicable."@en ;
                      :eratvIndex "4.10.10" ;
                      :inSkosConceptScheme <http://data.europa.eu/949/concepts/contact-strip-materials/ContactStripMaterials> ;
                      :legalDeadline "In accordance with Implementing Decision 2014/880/EU and by 16 March 2019 at the latest"@en ;
                      :rinfIndex "1.1.1.2.3.4" ;
                      :shaclShapeValidationRule <http://data.europa.eu/949/shapes/ContactStripMaterialApplicability> ,
                                                <http://data.europa.eu/949/shapes/ContactStripMaterialSKOS> ;
                      :usedInRCCCalculations "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
                      <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2020-08-25"^^xsd:date ;
                      <http://purl.org/dc/terms/modified> "2021-09-12"^^xsd:date ,
                                                          "2024-09-25"^^xsd:date ,
                                                          "2025-02-28"^^xsd:date ;
                      <http://purl.org/dc/terms/relation> :contactLineSystemType ;
                      rdfs:comment "Indication of which contact strip materials are permitted to be used."@en ;
                      rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://data.europa.eu/949/> ;
                      rdfs:label "Permitted contact strip material"@en ;
                      rdfs:seeAlso "LOC&PAS TSI: 4.2.8.2.9.4.2" ;
                      <http://www.w3.org/2003/06/sw-vocab-status/ns#term_status> "stable" ;
                      <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> """[NN] for impregnated carbon concern the metallic content in %. In case of selection of this option, the respective value of the metallic content has to be added. [NN] is the maximum percentage allowed.

In case of permitted material different than specified in predefined list, send ERA a change request.

When more than one value of the parameter has to be published, then parameter will to be repeated as many times as the number of values."""@en .


